From: mscharged-port
Subject: Tweak: a live replay catches up behind a catch-up screen
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

A spectator who joins a match under way plays it from its kickoff as fast
as the computer can (tweak patch 0086), and saw it race by. When that
catch-up begins more than 30 s behind, the host now shows a catch-up screen
instead (the score, how far it got, when it is live), and the match behind
it draws nothing, so its steps get nearly all of the time.

Drawing nothing is what a rollback's replay of a frame already does (tweak
patch 0042 and the sites before it): the places that only draw skip their
work, the updates around them still run. They now ask
mscharged_tweak_draws_nothing, which is true for a rollback's replay and
for a replay behind the catch-up screen. The sites that read the pads,
serve disc reads or send messages during a rollback's replay keep asking
mscharged_rollback_resimulating.

Behind the screen the steps also record no frames for the goal replays
(ReplayManager::GrabSnapshot) until the last 10 s before it is live:
nothing in the match reads them, only the goal replays (skipped while it
catches up) and the drawing. The goal replays after it is live find their
last seconds. On a production game, 355 s of the match caught up in
about 8 s instead of about 12 s, with every recorded checksum the same.

